# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Never publish: saved D&D Beyond listing pages.
# ~140 MB of copyrighted WotC content, and the input to extract_spells.py.
# The spell list derived from it (data/wizard-spells.csv) IS committed; the
# source pages are not. See "Rebuilding the spell list" in README.md.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
TheMasterSpellbook/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Never publish: the rendered table tent.
# make_table_tent.py --url embeds a live Google Form link, and the rendered PDF
# carries it in a link annotation. Ignore the PDF by extension so a stray render
# under any name cannot be committed by accident.
#
# build/table-tent.html IS committed, but only in its blank-placeholder state:
# re-run `python scripts/make_table_tent.py` with no --url to reset it before
# committing. SETUP.md step 4 says the same.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.pdf

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Never publish: Microsoft Office lock / owner files.
# Created while a workbook or document is open, and they contain the NAME of
# whoever has it open. One was committed by accident; hence the explicit rule.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
~$*

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
*.egg-info/

# Editors / OS
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
